  <h1>Indoor plant lighting</h1>
  <p class="prose">
    Light is food for a plant. Too little and growth stalls, leaves pale,
    and the plant slowly weakens. Too much direct sun and leaves scorch.
    Most houseplants do best in bright, indirect light — near a window, but
    out of the harsh midday sun.
  </p>
  <div class="scope-box">
    <p>
      <strong>What this page is:</strong> a lighting hub — the basics, plus
      links to the four deep guides below. It is not a deep guide itself.
      For light by window direction, read
      <a href="/guides/snake-plant-light-needs/">Snake Plant Light Needs Explained</a>;
      for low light only, read
      <a href="/guides/snake-plant-low-light/">Snake Plant Low Light</a> or
