      ranked list, read
      <a href="/guides/plants-that-grow-in-the-dark/">Plants That Grow in the Dark</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What "low light" really means</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    "Low light" on a plant label means the plant tolerates a dim spot — not
    that it prefers one. A plant in low light grows slowly and drinks less
    water, so it is easier to overwater there. No plant grows in true
    darkness; even the toughest low-light plants need some daylight to
    photosynthesise. A north-facing window or a spot a few metres from a
    bright window counts as low light. A windowless bathroom does not.
  </p>

